  "keys": "აბგდევთილმნორსუხ",
  "grammar": {
    "explain": [
      "Six new letters, and with them the words for the family. Two of them need attention: თ is a *t* with a little puff of air, as in English, and ხ is a sound English doesn't have.",
      {
        "h": "New letters"
      },
      {
        "letters": [
          {
            "letter": "ბ",
            "latin": "b",
            "say": "like the b in bed",
            "word": "ბებია",
            "word_latin": "bebia",
            "meaning": "grandmother"
          },
          {
            "letter": "გ",
            "latin": "g",
            "say": "like the g in go, always hard",
            "word": "გული",
            "word_latin": "guli",
            "meaning": "heart"
          },
          {
            "letter": "დ",
            "latin": "d",
            "say": "like the d in dog",
            "word": "დედა",
            "word_latin": "deda",
            "meaning": "mother"
          },
          {
            "letter": "ვ",
            "latin": "v",
            "say": "like the v in van",
            "word": "ვაშლი",
            "word_latin": "vashli",
            "meaning": "apple"
          },
          {
            "letter": "თ",
            "latin": "t",
            "say": "like the t in top, with a puff of air",
            "word": "თბილისი",
            "word_latin": "tbilisi",
            "meaning": "Tbilisi"
          },
          {
            "letter": "ხ",
            "latin": "kh",
            "say": "like the ch in Scottish loch",
            "word": "ხე",
            "word_latin": "khe",
            "meaning": "tree"
          }
        ],
        "lang": "ka"
      },
      {
        "h": "Watch out"
      },
      {
        "ul": [
          "გ (*g*) is always hard, as in *go*, also before ე and ი: გიტარა is *gitara* (guitar).",
          "ხ (*kh*) is the sound at the end of Scottish *loch* or German *Bach*: breathe out through a narrow throat.",
          "დ (*d*) and და: the word და means *and* and also *sister*."
        ]
      },
      {
        "h": "Try reading"
      },
      "Read each word aloud, then tap it to check.",
      {
        "flash": [
          [
            "დედა",
            "deda",
            "mother"
          ],
          [
            "ბებია",
            "bebia",
            "grandmother"
          ],
          [
            "ბაბუა",
            "babua",
            "grandfather"
          ],
          [
            "და",
            "da",
            "and; sister"
          ],
          [
            "თბილისი",
            "tbilisi",
            "Tbilisi"
          ],
          [
            "ხე",
            "khe",
            "tree"
          ],
          [
            "გული",
            "guli",
            "heart"
          ],
          [
            "ვარდი",
            "vardi",
            "rose"
          ]
        ],
        "lang": "ka"
      }
    ]
  },
